    "done_when": "Jev is blind to codex budget state in production. Since merge 77fad8331, dispatch-path picks fill codex candidates from a recorded account-window reading. Every one of the 184 codex offers since then carries budget_reason \"no recorded account-window reading for budget group codex-sub\", with burn_multiple, pace_allowance and utilisation all null. The paid-lane document the publisher writes (reckon/crew/paid_lanes.py; ~/public/reckon/paid-lanes.json, written about every 5 min by reckon-paid-lanes.timer, and fresh at 81 s old when checked) lists every account, codex, codex-astra and codex-luna included, as state \"unknown\" with null windows and source None. Codex-family accounts are supposed to carry source \"rollout\". The coordinator's unverified hypothesis: the worker write fence now gives each run its own harness home, so codex session rollouts no longer land in ~/.codex/sessions, where the publisher looks. Confirm or refute this by measurement before changing anything.\n\n1. Diagnose: find where paid_lanes reads codex readings, where codex rollouts with rate-limit or window data are actually written today (the main ~/.codex/sessions and per-run harness homes under ~/.config/reckon/crew/runs/*/), and why the document reads unknown. Record the evidence in docs/evidence/fragments/one-typesafe-model-picker/paid-lanes-codex-window.html.\n2. Restore real codex window readings in the paid-lane document, with observed_at and source, from wherever the freshest trustworthy reading now lives. Prefer the newest rollout across the main home and run harness homes, bounded to a recent window so a scan stays cheap. Never run a live account probe from the publisher if that costs a codex call on every timer tick; if a probe is the only source, rate-limit it and say so.\n3. Make the dispatch-path picker read the codex window from the paid-lane document, through paid_lanes.read_document, which preflight already uses, carrying the reading's age and marking it stale past its shelf life. Prove it with a test: a fixture paid-lane document with a codex-sub reading yields the same burn_multiple, pace_allowance and utilisation on the dispatch-path codex candidates as a standalone pick computes from the same reading. A document whose accounts are unknown keeps the named budget_reason.\n4. After the change, run the publisher once by hand (its CLI main) and show the document's codex account carrying a real reading. Then run `reckon crew pick --project reckon --role implement --spec-level guided --goal G --done-when W` and show the codex candidates carrying burn and pace.\n\nGate: new tests in tests/test_paid_lanes_codex_window.py, tests/test_picker_dispatch_pace.py, tests/test_paid_lanes*.py, tests/test_budget*.py and tests/test_picker*.py. Run them with the main checkout's .venv/bin/python -m pytest -p no:cacheprovider -n 8 in the FOREGROUND, with one log for base and one for head under the run directory, each ending in an EXIT line, judged by delta.",
